# CLI Command Patterns

## CLI Entry Point

The main CLI is defined in [bin/koapp.js](mdc:bin/koapp.js) and provides:

- `koapp init <app-name>` - Initialize new project
- `koapp http [dir]` - Serve a static directory over HTTP
- `koapp skills -i <cursor|claude>` - Install the bundled AI skills into a project

## Command Structure

Commands are implemented in the `commands/` directory and auto-loaded by
`@axiosleo/cli-tool` through the `commands_dir` option:

- [commands/init.js](mdc:commands/init.js) - Project initialization
- [commands/http.js](mdc:commands/http.js) - Static HTTP server
- [commands/skills.js](mdc:commands/skills.js) - AI skills installer

Shared, testable helpers live in `src/cli/` (e.g. [src/cli/pnpm.js](mdc:src/cli/pnpm.js)
for Corepack / pnpm detection, [src/cli/pkg.js](mdc:src/cli/pkg.js) for
package-manager detection). Keep command files thin and put logic there.

## Project Initialization

The init command asks which template to generate (or takes `-t`):

```bash
npx @axiosleo/koapp init <app-name> [-d <optional-dir>] [-t simple-ts|simple-js|monorepo]
```

| Template | Source | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `simple-ts` (default) | `assets/simple/ts/` | One TypeScript HTTP service and sample routes. No database. |
| `simple-js` | `assets/simple/js/` | The same service in CommonJS. No compile step. |
| `monorepo` | `assets/monorepo/` | pnpm workspace: `apps/services` (admin Session auth, `/openapi` Bearer Api-Key, SQLite), `packages/commands`, `bin/<app-name>.js` |

Every template also receives `.agents/skills/` copied from `assets/skills/`.
After writing files, init probes for pnpm (offering to install the pinned
version) and then offers to run `pnpm install` and `pnpm dev`.

Template selection and file rendering live in [src/cli/scaffold.js](mdc:src/cli/scaffold.js)
so they can be tested without a prompt.

## Template System

Templates use the `.tmpl` extension and are processed during project generation:

- `assets/simple/{ts,js}/**/*.tmpl` and `assets/monorepo/**/*.tmpl` - rendered
  with `_render_with_file`, which replaces `${name}` with the app name; the
  `.tmpl` suffix is stripped on output
- `assets/monorepo/bin/monoapp.js.tmpl` - renamed to `bin/<app-name>.js`
  (monorepo template only)
- `assets/skills/` - copied verbatim into `<app>/.agents/skills/`
  (`_sync` reback must stay off, or the copy writes back into this package)

## Command Development

When creating new CLI commands:

1. Create command file in `commands/` directory
2. Extend base Command class from `@axiosleo/cli-tool`
3. Implement `exec(args, options)` method
4. No manual registration is needed - every file under `commands/` is picked up
   via `commands_dir` in `bin/koapp.js`

## Usage Examples

```bash
# Initialize new project (prompts for a template; default is simple-ts)
npx @axiosleo/koapp init my-app

# Skip the prompt
npx @axiosleo/koapp init my-app -t simple-js
npx @axiosleo/koapp init my-app -t monorepo

# Initialize in a specific directory
npx @axiosleo/koapp init my-app -d ./projects

# Show help
npx @axiosleo/koapp init -h
```
